The `memcmp` function is not guaranteed to be constant-time; its execution time can vary based on the data being compared, particularly it may return early when a difference is found. This side-channel allows an attacker to perform a timing attack to guess the valid MAC byte by byte, eventually forging a correct MD5 signature and bypassing authentication.

